National Security Council. Those who have worked under Landholm, who in no way shed tears over what he is facing now.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:15.680
They also say, quite far back in time, that this is a very difficult job.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:19.300
And it is actually unreasonable that he stands by himself in it.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:24.620
When there have been political services before, there has been a State Secretary, there are often other structures.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.600
Here it seems to have been a little smaller.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:29.530
or

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:34.840
Some people have reacted to that. So it's not just Landerholm's story.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:38.940
All of these are events where Henrik Landerholm himself...

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:47.440
He's the one who forgets his phone, he's the one who forgets his note, and he's the one who forgets his documents in his hotel room.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:49.080
And he's the one who's on the spot in court.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.560
The Moderates, in any case, have been able to joke about this.

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:59.900
It was a bit weird during the Sweden meeting, because Landerholm wasn't just Ulf Kristersson's...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:10.360
He is a childhood friend, he is also the brother of party secretary Karin Enström and it was one of the top moderates who joked before that think about the big dinner, get the assignment.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:14.770
Look under the counter, there is a forgotten secret document.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:19.500
But it might have been a bit too much self-irony, even for the moderates.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.290
Now they seem to be able to joke around a bit.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:25.970
This was in March, so this was before a lot had happened.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:29.770
Right, but when I've talked to news reporters...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.600
and you probably have similar experiences, when everything is besieged and you start writing about it.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:39.010
These press secretaries were completely hysterical, they called in time and time again,

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:43.230
they had opinions about subheadings, picture texts, it never ended.

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:48.870
It was a panicked organization, that's how I've got it described to me. How have you experienced it?

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:52.810
An incredibly sensitive issue, the Jellövsta incident.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:58.500
President, try to respond as little as possible. Try to protect...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.100
Bye!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.030
The top, as much as you can.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.090
And when it comes to institutions, it's the Kursgården?

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:04.870
The Kursgården, yes.

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:06.390
Don't you conclude that yourself?

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:08.480
on Twitter X.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:13.780
In one way or another. Or at least he broke you there and thought he might handle it that way.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.340
He was the first one to tell me about it.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.860
It's misleading, which we have also shown.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.900
It contains several mistakes.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:24.000
And that also makes it the government's own explanation of it all.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:27.180
Based on how you answered, it feels like you maybe, maybe, felt it.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:27.780
Thank you.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:28.500
In some way.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.060
Can't say.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:34.120
But the government council has also been a subject of your investigation.

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.290
–Absolutely. –How did they manage this?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:43.320
It's very difficult to deal with. All of our questions are interpreted, so we have to ask them over and over again.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.200
All of our requests are interpreted, so we have to ask them over and over again.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:50.940
It takes a very long time to get documents out. For example, we've had to wait...

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.040
We spent 45 days on simple documents to submit.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:59.360
In the end we used a pseudonym to test it.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.880
that we had proposed.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:05.880
We got the same email logs with pseudonyms in two days, digitally.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:14.800
The others we had to wait for over six weeks and had to go back and forth to the government office's research room, stand outside and come in.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:17.220
and get them escorted by a guard to take action.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:21.360
And then we have to do it over and over again. So all the time, a lot of fighting.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.560
Let's hear what some loud voices have to say about this.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.590
In general, one can say that it gives a bit of an Åsa Nisse impression.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:38.230
Yes, you have to note that the Social Democrats tend to be more skilful in getting this kind of thing to disappear from the debate.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:44.890
I mean, in the case of the Transport Board, it was in a way still serious because then there was actually an intention to round up.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.280
the legislation for running this IT project.

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:51.800
But that was managed to be quite small in the media,

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:54.900
simply by changing a couple of ministers' positions

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:55.980
and then saying,

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.060
now we have taken responsibility for Sweden.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:21:59.050
And that was it.

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:07.340
That type of media management does not have the right experience to do so, and therefore these things get bigger.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:12.940
Would you say that it is a unique event in Swedish security policy history?

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:14.980
How do you mean he's here?

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:15.720
Thank you.

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:19.670
First, in the third attempt, we managed to put in a national security guard.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:24.130
Well, that hasn't happened before, so in that sense it's unique.

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:27.930
All government heads end up with unexpected events.

00:22:28.310 --> 00:22:29.190
It's about that...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.120
You should not overdo the equity of it, but it is important to make sure that there are not too many.

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:42.820
There has been a certain indecision, I think. A fairly large indecision in at least a couple of cases.

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:49.090
Both around Landerholm and Anakimbe Batra. And you should have been faster there.

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:56.500
I think when you talk to moderators now, who are also members of the government council,

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:59.960
it sounds a bit like this is a question that...

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:06.210
Both internally, but also the voters may have already drawn consequences of it.

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:08.310
We'll have to see if he gets convicted.

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:11.570
On the other hand, I think it might be easier to do it for themselves.

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:16.110
There is a KU investigation that is waiting for this case to be resolved.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:17.190
The Constitutional Court of Justice.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:22.210
Exactly. And they are interested in what the prime minister knew.

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:25.450
When did the prime minister know? How did they handle this?

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:29.970
I was in on this before, when he talked about what he had for backup in the parliament.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:36.020
And that's what makes him live on, because then the media will attack him.

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:38.800
And he can live all the way into the election campaign.

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:40.300
He definitely can.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:48.640
No matter how it goes in the court of law, it is quite likely that there will also be a court trial of this.

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:51.140
And that is a few months ahead.

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:57.440
The KU investigation is paused as long as this criminal case goes on.

00:23:57.440 --> 00:23:59.980
And that's first after we have a law...

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:16.090
The opposition has no reason to speed up the investigation. They want to have this as close to the election as possible.

00:24:16.770 --> 00:24:23.890
This is not a question that determines the election. The voters consider other things to be more important.

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:29.970
But I think it affects the image of government decency, and that is a problem for Kristina.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.580
It will be difficult for him to get into the election.

00:24:32.880 --> 00:24:34.720
Listen, we have a viewer question.

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:41.500
It sounds like this.

00:24:41.560 --> 00:24:48.680
It's an anonymous person who wonders if there are things that authorities keep from the prime minister.

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:49.780
Just because they are secret.

00:24:50.060 --> 00:24:52.160
It's up to you, Hugo. It feels like you could know this.

00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:55.160
Now I'm thinking about this case.

00:24:55.580 --> 00:24:59.620
But here, when you talk to Ulf Kristersson, for example, about what he knew...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.040
When we asked him what information he had received, it was very clear that he didn't know anything until it was clarified.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:11.580
He said that he didn't know if he knew when we asked him if he knew about the post he published.

00:25:12.320 --> 00:25:21.080
It is clear that there is a gap between what you tell the prime minister and not, just because he may not know certain things.

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:29.940
That's right. A state secretary once said that a state secretary's most important job is sometimes to keep his minister a bit unaware of the situation.

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:36.000
Now I think you're slipping a little from the question. Does a prime minister know everything despite the fact that it's a secret?

00:25:36.160 --> 00:25:46.080
I think we should almost be a jurist to answer that. But if I understand correctly, the prime minister should be able to know what the prime minister needs to know.

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:51.860
Then there are certainly limitations in secrecy and there are certainly people who will limit what they want to tell.

00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:56.680
There are, for example, identities of agents and so on that you don't even sit and talk about verbally.

00:25:57.220 --> 00:25:59.980
But I believe that you should have the right to do what you need to do.

00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:05.460
And if you have more questions, you can post them here.

00:26:05.870 --> 00:26:06.590
Don't send them to me.

00:26:07.690 --> 00:26:23.090
Let's take a look at Landerholm's spotify lists and see if we can find something that feels exciting.

00:26:23.350 --> 00:26:26.170
You've got a leaf under, and you can...

00:26:26.170 --> 00:26:28.270
If you just look quickly...

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:34.650
Yes, we forgive him and it feels like he could go to the same party as Billström.

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:45.350
If I may note one thing first, I really don't know much about this, but I don't see any heavy industrial techno that you listen to in Berlin.

00:26:45.630 --> 00:26:50.390
It should be said that he had a lot of playlists. We have chosen new unheard.

00:26:50.630 --> 00:26:54.320
And all playlists that are public are up until 2021.

00:26:54.780 --> 00:26:59.610
He may have done a lot more and then they became secret, but it may well exist.

00:27:00.510 --> 00:27:02.410
To Hans, or to your answer?

00:27:02.650 --> 00:27:15.000
After a quick eye examination, I'm of the opinion that Herr Landerholm has a much more developed taste in music than Random Moderat.

00:27:15.100 --> 00:27:17.520
He is genuinely interested in music.

00:27:17.740 --> 00:27:26.800
Here we have everything from Marcus Krunegård to Miles Davis and Johnny Mitchell and Harry Nilsson and Harry Styles.

00:27:26.800 --> 00:27:29.420
Yes, this is a well-composed...

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:38.830
A list of different eras, without a doubt a person who is interested in music who has put this together.

00:27:38.970 --> 00:27:46.950
I think it signals a little more that this is music that he has in his lures when he's out and running and listening to Cardi B or Swedish House Mafia.

00:27:47.190 --> 00:27:48.850
But without you with Harry Nilsson.

00:27:49.110 --> 00:27:53.650
Not just that, but several of the other songs he wants to get up on stage.

00:27:53.890 --> 00:27:59.970
Who knows, one of these songs may become the theme song for the film about Sweden's first national anthem.

00:28:00.900 --> 00:28:15.460
This case really has everything for a really good thriller, above all that it is slowly rising, it goes up to the top, to the power, to the prime minister in this case, what does he know or not.

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:24.400
Everything there is tickling, the security of the country, can it be bigger than that? If it was a very nasty series of court, then I would think we would see it as the document.
